# Parallel worktree subagents
When a task parallelizes, fan out with `Agent(isolation: "worktree")` - each
subagent gets its own worktree under the repo's `.claude/worktrees/`, all in
this one sandbox. That isolation ALREADY puts the subagent's cwd under
`.claude/worktrees/...` before it starts - a subagent finding itself there
should NOT ALSO call `EnterWorktree`; doing so nests yet another, unnecessary
worktree layer, and if that subagent itself fans out further subagents that
make the same mistake, depth compounds fast. node_modules is hydrated
automatically when the worktree is created, so don't run `npm install` or
treat the worktree as having no deps. Keep the parallel phase network-quiet:
adding a NEW dependency needs the npm registry and will trip the egress gate,
so do dependency changes before/after fanning out, not during. Use the
directory named in `$CSANDBOX_SCRATCH` for handoffs between agents.
